        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:deb/debian/mount@2.41.5-0%2Bdeb13u1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "pkg:deb/debian/util-linux@2.41.5-0%2Bdeb13u1"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "inline_mitigations_already_exist",
      "impact_statement": "The flaw lets an unprivileged user reach privileged mount operations through the setuid mount(8). The image removes every setuid and setgid bit, so mount runs with the rights of the caller, and /etc/fstab has no entries. The app runs as the unprivileged user app and never starts mount."
    },
